-- title:
--   Coordinate point derivations in the Cartier dual of 𝔽ₚ ⊗ R
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$, let $\mathbb{Z}/p$ carry an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure whose structure map has kernel the ideal $(p)$ of $\mathcal{O}$, and assume $\mathcal{O}$ is $(p)$-adically complete. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal{O}$, that is, $d$ power series $F_i$ in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \sqcup \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant term, linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each block, and satisfying associativity, and assume $F$ is commutative in the sense that interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each $F_i$. Let $v \ge 1$, and let $R$ be a commutative ring that is a Hopf algebra over $\mathcal{O}$ and free of finite rank as an $\mathcal{O}$-module. Let $\pi : \mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] \to R$ be a surjective $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of the ideal $pR$, such that $\pi$ coincides with $(p)$-adic evaluation at the tuple $(\pi(X_i))_i$ on every power series, and such that $\ker \pi$ is generated by the $d$ components of $F$'s $p^v$-fold iterate series (defined recursively by $0$ at stage $0$ and by substituting the previous stage into the first block of $F$ at each step). Assume finally that for each $i$ the comultiplication of $\pi(X_i)$ equals the $(p)$-adic evaluation in $R \otimes_{\mathcal{O}} R$ of $F_i$ at the tuple $(\pi(X_j) \otimes 1, 1 \otimes \pi(X_j))_j$. Then there exist $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear functionals $D_1,\dots,D_d$ on $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{\mathcal{O}} R$, viewed as elements of the Cartier dual (the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear dual of that bialgebra), with $D_i(1 \otimes \pi(X_j)) = \delta_{ij}$ and obeying the $\varepsilon$-derivation law $D_i(ab) = D_i(a)\,\varepsilon(b) + \varepsilon(a)\,D_i(b)$ for all $a,b$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit over $\mathbb{Z}/p$.
--
--   The functionals produced here are the point derivations at the origin of the mod $p$ fibre of the $p^v$-torsion subscheme of $F$, taken along the coordinates $\pi(X_j)$; the hypothesis $v \ge 1$ is what makes the coordinates augmentation-zero modulo $p$. The result feeds the comparison of powers of these derivations with Hasse–Witt data in [`MvFormalGroup.exists_cartierDual_derivation_pow_eq_sum_hasseWitt_smul`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_cartierDual_derivation_pow_eq_sum_hasseWitt_smul).
